  "report_period": "Week 47 (13th Nov to 20th Nov 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Ever Beauty\" 180/2011 Qingdao Beihai, China (SS 07/2031, DD 8/2029, Scrubber fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at high USD 39 mill basis delivery Jan-Apr'27, while the sister vessel \"Ever Ability\" 180/2011 Qingdao Beihai, China (SS 10/2031, DD 10/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed to clients of H-Line at high USD 39 mill basis delivery Dec'26- Mar'27. Note that in October, the one-year-younger \"Ekaterini V\" 173/2012 Bohai, China (SS/DD 01/2027) was sold at USD 35 mill. The Post Panamax \"Auriga Ocean\" 93/2008 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 08/2031, DD 08/2029) was committed to undisclosed interests at xs USD 15 mill. For reference, the three-years-younger \"Maritime King\" 95/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS 02/2031, DD 04/2029) was sold a month ago at USD 19,2 mill. On the Kamsarmax sector, Ta-Ho Maritime committed their \"Taho Australia\" 81/2019 Oshima, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 09/2027) at high USD 38 mill. By way of comparison, the \"Babitonga\" 81/2019 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 10/2027) was sold in early October at USD 38,5 mill basis delivery Feb'27. MUR Shipping have committed their Handysize \"African Owl\" 34/2016 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 01/2031, DD 12/2028) to Turkish interests at USD 21,5 mill. Remind you that back in July, the one-year-older sister vessel \"African Piper\" 34/2015 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 01/2030, DD 07/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 20 mill. Moreover, the \"ABK Tiger\" 28/2002 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 02/2027) was sold at USD 5,3 mill, while the one-year- older \"Duyen Hai 1\" 28/2001 Kanda, Japan (SS 02/2031, DD 06/2029) was sold at USD 5,5 mill. For reference, the younger \"HTK Lucky\" 28/2003 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 06/2027) was sold back in July at rgn USD 6 mill.",
    "tankers": "Pan Ocean have committed their MR2 \"Grand Ace6\" 46/2007 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 20,5 mill. Remind you that back in September, the \"Rui Fu Sheng\" 46/2007 Sungdong, Korea (SS 01/2031, DD 01/2029) was sold at xs USD 19 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route softened slightly, with Dampier and Port Hedland fixtures settling between USD 13.40/14.30 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, held steady levels between USD 35.00/35.50 fio, while a Port Cartier departure to Qingdao hit USD 48.50 fio. Transatlantic trade saw a Seven Islands run to Rotterdam fix at USD 15.50 fio. In regional trades, Teluk Rubiah to Qingdao achieved USD 11.20 fio, while coastal Indian business from Visakhapatnam to Hazira made USD 7.00 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with Singapore-Japan options settled between USD 19,000/21,000 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan, India and Singapore-Japan ranges fetched between USD 21,500/26,000 pd. Indonesian coal runs to China, SE Asia and India ranges achieved between USD 13,000/20,000 pd, alongside coastal Indian iron ore trips from ECI to WCI fixing between USD 21,000/22,000 pd. From India, trips via ECSA to Singapore-Japan and Persian Gulf ranges fixed between USD 17,000/21,000 pd, while a direct ECSA front-haul reached USD 21,500 pd alongside an $800,000 ballast bonus. In the Atlantic, Continent departures via USEC made USD 28,000 pd to India and USD 17,250 pd on a transatlantic round. On period, two Kamsarmaxes delivering in North China fixed for 9 to 12 months duration between USD 19,260/21,500 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, Indonesian coal trips to China, SE Asia and ECI ranges settled between USD 15,500/21,000 pd, while an Australian round within SE Asia fetched USD 23,250 pd. A South China departure to ECI reached USD 30,000 pd and a two-laden-leg trip from North China with Singapore-Japan redelivery achieved USD 24,000 pd. Long-haul runs from North China to West Africa fixed between USD 25,100/25,250 pd, whereas a North China trip to US Gulf made USD 19,000 pd. Out of West Coast India, a trip via Persian Gulf to ECI settled at USD 14,000 pd. In the Atlantic, Continent scrap to East Med obtained USD 32,000 pd, while a West Africa front-haul departure to North China fixed at USD 17,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Pacific, a long-haul trip from Japan to US Gulf fixed at USD 22,000 pd. In the Atlantic, ECSA grain runs to WCSA achieved strong levels between USD 32,600/35,000 pd, while departures to USEC and US Gulf made USD 32,000 pd and USD 25,000 pd respectively. Out of US Gulf, grain trips to NCSA settled between USD 19,000/24,000 pd, alongside a transatlantic run to Continent at USD 21,750 pd. From Continent, grains to West Africa reached USD 26,000 pd, whereas a lumber trip to US Gulf fixed at USD 19,000 pd."
    }
  },
